    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 26 tests pass, including the checkpoints affected by this change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence, in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **`nextCustomerCode`** now takes both `city` and `lastName`. It builds `CITY3` (upper-cased first three letters of the city) and `LAST3` (upper-cased first three of the last name), and computes `NNNN` as a 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to **one more than the number of owners already in that same city** (matched case-insensitively via the existing `normalizeForHousehold` helper).\n- Added a small `prefixThree` helper for the shared \"upper-cased first three letters\" logic.\n- Updated the call site to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\nEverything derived from `customerCode` rebuilds automatically: `Owner.getMembershipNumber()` already formats `\"%s-M%02d\"` from `customerCode`, so it now carries the city prefix without any change there (verified by Cp14).\n\nNo migration of stored data was needed \u2014 the change is at generation time, and the tests are transactional/black-box over the create+read endpoints.",
